  "title": "Sony Data Discman / Electronic Book Player",
  "year": "1990",
  "subtitle": "The first dedicated e-book reader, three years before the word meant anything",
  "why_scout_cares": "A purpose-built portable CD-ROM reader with a QWERTY keyboard and Yes/No prompt-driven search — the interaction model of the e-reader category, born in 1990 and dead in the West. One unit sits in the permanent collection of the Victoria and Albert Museum.",
  "search_terms": ["Sony Data Discman", "DD-1", "Electronic Book Player", "EBXA", "e-book 1990"],
